UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventcentennialfilmseries3athecocoanuts192925972-20261003@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261002T161342Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261003
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261004
SUMMARY:CENTENNIAL FILM Series: The Cocoanuts (1929)
DESCRIPTION:The Cocoanuts is a staple of early sound-era comedy. Set in a struggling Florida hotel during a real estate boom\, the film follows Groucho Marx as the fast-talking hotel owner attempting to sell swampland properties while managing a steady stream of eccentric guests. Chaos quickly ensues as Chico Marx’s con-artist schemes and Harpo Marx’s silent mischief disrupt every deal and conversation. Blending vaudeville-style humor with early musical sequences\, The Cocoanuts showcases the Marx Brothers’ signature anarchic comedy\, rapid-fire wordplay\, and slapstick timing. Featuring songs by Irving Berlin\, the film reflects the transitional moment between silent cinema and “talkies\,” establishing the brothers as major comedic forces in Hollywood and laying the groundwork for their later classic films. STARS: Groucho Marx\, Harpo Marx\, Zeppo Marx\, Chico Marx\, Margaret Dumont RUNTIME: 93 minutes GENRE: Comedy\, Musical This show is part of the Weinberg Center’s Centennial Film Event\, celebrating 100 years of screenings in our historic building. The Weinberg Center\, located in the heart of Downtown Frederick\, MD\, offers a historic backdrop and timeless atmosphere for a unique film experience.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/centennial-film-series%3a-the-cocoanuts-(1929)/25972/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventcentennialkickoff25955-20261003@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261002T161342Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261003
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261004
SUMMARY:Centennial Kickoff
DESCRIPTION:Help us launch the Centennial Season with an afternoon of celebration at the Weinberg Center. We’re opening our doors for a free open house event filled with live entertainment\, silent film shorts\, family-friendly activities\, door prizes\, and more. Drop by anytime from 12 pm to 4 pm to explore Frederick’s unique historic theater\, connect with the community\, and discover all the exciting experiences the upcoming season has in store. Whether you’re a longtime patron or discovering the Weinberg for the first time\, there will be something for everyone to enjoy! This is a free event that is open to the public and does not require a ticket. This show is part of the Weinberg Center’s Centennial Events\, celebrating 100 years of entertainment in our historic building. The Weinberg Center\, located in the heart of Downtown Frederick\, MD\, offers a historic backdrop and timeless atmosphere for a meaningful entertainment experience.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/centennial-kickoff/25955/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventcivilwarwalkingtour17630-20261003@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261002T161342Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261003
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
SUMMARY:Civil War Walking Tour
DESCRIPTION:Explore what it was like to live in Frederick during the Civil War. Stories include the last Confederate invasion of the North\, the ransom of Frederick\, and the Battle of Monocacy. *Tour starts at the Museum of Frederick County History\, 24 East Church Street\, Frederick\, MD 21701
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/civil-war-walking-tour/17630/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventcuriousiguanapresents3alocalchildrensauthormelindabeatty25905-20261003@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261002T161342Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261003
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261004
SUMMARY:Curious Iguana Presents: Local Children's Author Melinda Beatty
DESCRIPTION:We are delighted to celebrate our very own bookseller and local author Melinda Beatty on Saturday\, October 3 from 11:30 am-12:30 pm at C. Burr Artz Public Library. Join us for storytime with Mel\, where she will read her new book\, What Is a Pirate? Following the reading\, enjoy a fun craft with the author! Mel will also be available to sign books. Copies of What Is a Pirate? will be available for purchase at the event. Location: the Children’s Programming Room at C. Burr Artz Public Library\, 110 E. Patrick Street\, Frederick\, MD\, 21701 This event is free and open to the public. We are proud to partner with Frederick County Public Libraries for this event. For accessibility requests\, email events@curiousiguana.com at least two (2) weeks prior to the event. About the book: From the team that brought you The Witch's Table comes another hilarious and charming story about what exactly makes a pirate a pirate! I am a pirate\, so I guess pirates do. The crew aboard the Leaky Sneaker is filled with the piratey-est pirates ever to sail the seven seas. Which is why Captain Bogbrush has no idea what to do with Montague Frippington von Fancypants. Montague wears petticoats while sailing\, takes pearl necklaces as booty\, and politely plunders on raids. Pirates don't do that! Or can Montague help the captain understand that there is more to being a pirate than what he might believe? About the author: Melinda Beatty has had years of practice trying to explain to others why she was just having an imaginary conversation between two people that don't exist\, so becoming a writer seemed like the best way to stop everyone from looking at her funny. After years of narrowboat living on the English canals\, she and her British husband are now back on dry land in Maryland\, where by day\, she's a mild-mannered indie bookseller\, and by night\, she wrangles words\, crafts projects\, and raises a Labrador and two fierce miniwomen.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/curious-iguana-presents%3a-local-childrens-author-melinda-beatty/25905/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfallfestatrosehillmanorpark20706-20261003@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261002T161342Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261003
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:Fall Fest at Rose Hill Manor Park
DESCRIPTION:Join the Frederick County Farm Museum for a fall festival including agricultural demonstrations\, food\, hayrides\, crafts\, and more! Be sure to complete the Agriculture Olympics on Saturday with the University of Maryland Extension Office of Frederick County. On Sunday the Farm Museum will host the Kids' Pedal Pull at 1pm.
