DTSTAMP:20261002T161342Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261023
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261024
SUMMARY:Guided Exhibit Tours
DESCRIPTION:Experience the Museum of Frederick County History through a guided tour. Join the staff and volunteers who curated our 2026 exhibits as they explore our various galleries. Each tour is a unique experience based on the interests of the group and what special things staff wants to highlight that week. Descriptions of each week's tour can be found on the Heritage Frederick website\, which includes accessibility notes. Tours are included with admission!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/guided-exhibit-tours/25817/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventjamiekayefirstfridays25206-20261023@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261002T161342Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261023
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261024
SUMMARY:Jamie Kaye First Fridays
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Jamie Kaye’s First Fridays at Sandbox! Jamie is an incredibly talented local sensation who has played at venues all over Frederick and the surrounding area. She’ll be at Sandbox playing her high energy\, all star set including current and classic hits\, sprinkled in originals\, AND a little birdie told us she takes song requests. Jamie ALWAYS brings a fun time - you won’t want to miss it!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/jamie-kaye-first-fridays/25206/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventjumbospumpkinpatchfallfestival11483-20261023@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261002T161342Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261023
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261024
SUMMARY:Jumbo's Pumpkin Patch Fall Festival
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the season with a full day of festive fun for all ages at Jumbo’s Pumpkin Patch! From classic farm adventures to fall-themed attractions\, our Fall Fun Festival is the perfect weekend outing for families\, friends\, and pumpkin lovers. What’s Included with Admission: Your ticket includes unlimited access to a variety of seasonal attractions: Hayrides through the farm 30+ acre u-pick pumpkin patch (pumpkins sold by the pound) Corn maze (14 acres) Petting zoo Jumping pillow Giant slides Mini mazes for younger guests Playgrounds and yard games General Store with fall shopping and décor​ Optional Add-Ons: (Available for Purchase Onsite - Saturday and Sunday Only) Enhance your day with these fun extras: Pony Rides – $7 Face Painting – $4 Sandy Candy (Edible Sand Art) – $4 Corn Cannon – $5 (3 shots) ​ Food & Drinks: Come hungry! A variety of food\, snacks\, and beverages are available for purchase\, including selections from Liquidity Ale Works of Mt. Airy. Tickets available online or at the gate.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/jumbos-pumpkin-patch-fall-festival/11483/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgevent2026exhibitsatmuseumoffrederickcountyhistory24908-20261024@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261002T161342Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261024
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261025
SUMMARY:2026 Exhibits at Museum of Frederick County History
DESCRIPTION:Take a deep dive into various topics that have defined Frederick's history\, as we celebrate America's 250th anniversary and our County's role in the Revolution. Featuring brand new exhibits: Cultivating Independence: Frederick in the Revolution Witnessing Revolution All Saints Street: Avenue to the History of Frederick and Its African American Community Growing Gold: A History of Frederick’s Goldfish Industry And returning favorites: Etchison Connections Timeless Toys 24 E Church Street Decorative Arts See our all new and renovated exhibits\, March 7\,2026 through December 12\, 2026. Buy tickets here.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/2026-exhibits-at-museum-of-frederick-county-history/24908/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventalleynights23158-20261024@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261002T161342Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261024
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261025
SUMMARY:Alley Nights
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to Alley Nights — your Saturday night destination in Downtown Frederick. With three bars open\, the party moves wherever the night takes you! Start in our newly renovated Main Bar\, catch the DJ spinning in Terrace\, or head upstairs to the rooftop bar for drinks and views of downtown Frederick. Add late-night bites\, great music\, and a lively crowd — and you’ve got everything you need for the perfect Saturday night! Benefactor Events joins us every first and third Saturday of the month to get the party going in Terrace! Meet us at Alley Nights! No cover | 21+ event.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/alley-nights/23158/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventfieldfreshfarmersmarket23988-20261024@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261002T161342Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261024
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261025
SUMMARY:Field Fresh Farmers Market
DESCRIPTION:Come visit the largest producer-only farmers market in Frederick County\, MD\, featuring over 30 local vendors! We're open every Saturday from April 25 to November 21\, 2026\, 9 am - 1 pm. See you there\, at the corner of E. Patrick St. & Franklin St.!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/field-fresh-farmers-market/23988/
END:VEVENT
